data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"post\": {\n      \"platform\": \"facebook\",\n      \"postId\": \"2817241591782952\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1723720494468406/posts/2817241591782952/\",\n      \"description\": \"Posting anonymous because our coaches retaliate against our kids for what we say.  \\nHere's my question,  what can you do if the coaches are trying to hold you back? \\nMy son has played football since he was 5. He can play every position and really well. He is just naturally athletic.  (Also played as pitcher, catcher and 3rd base on baseball,  played basketball,  soccer, wrestling,  lacrosse and always excelled). Football is his love and he wants to go pro so he gave up other sports and only fills in as guest player for tournaments in other sports off season as needed. He played offense and defense his freshman year staying in the whole game with no rest. He is a beast. He got to play a few varsity at the end of the year and has been a varsity starter sophomore and junior years. He has attended camps, combines, game day visits. He weight lifts. Puts film on Twitter and instagram.  Yet his coach won't promote him to scouts and said wait til next year. His senior year.  But they are promoting younger players (albeit they are specialty like running back, quarterback, kickers) who are now getting looked at.  \\nIt's really deflating for a young player who has always given 100%. It makes them feel not good enough.  \\nCoaches can make or break a player. Give them playtime or not. Get them scouted or overlooked.  \\nWhat can we do as parents? I feel helpless.\",\n      \"publishedAt\": \"2025-11-03T14:20:51.000Z\",\n      \"isPaidPartnership\": null,\n      \"sharedPostId\": null,\n      \"sharedPostUrl\": null,\n      \"feedbackId\": \"ZmVlZGJhY2s6cGZiaWQwMmRwaG9ZdXZXUUE4R3JRc1N5V1p6cHhncGtyOUFUNmlQdWFZbkxjVnBHaUpLMnNHRnFxbldnZ29QM0p5UzRyZHhs\",\n      \"linkAttachment\": null\n    },\n    \"author\": {\n      \"name\": \"Anonymous participant\",\n      \"profileUrl\": null,\n      \"avatarUrl\": \"https://scontent-iad3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35477-6/480704845_9249193088540936_1864352811635405115_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx160x160&ctp=s100x100&_nc_cat=1&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6f313d&_nc_ohc=dkVHLGVqEQMQ7kNvwHxu6vs&_nc_oc=AdqXhbfcsghdZdtbdwui4D0U8sLT-ByM5a-k10XGF5U3LRujDWOglSo1omL1wyvaJQ8&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.xx&_nc_gid=OJIIUvzSSSLAmeS-5Qd41w&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQStdlT6tpm32ayHsdEyiLoiaGG84eLbRYGGG7sCCoK9xg&oe=6AF3DA17\",\n      \"platformUserId\": \"681907418326945\",\n      \"verified\": false\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"likes\": 7,\n      \"comments\": 36,\n      \"shares\": 1,\n      \"views\": null,\n      \"reactions\": {\n        \"thankful\": 0,\n        \"like\": 6,\n        \"love\": 0,\n        \"care\": 1,\n        \"haha\": 0,\n        \"wow\": 0,\n        \"sad\": 0,\n        \"anger\": 0,\n        \"pride\": 0,\n        \"confused\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    \"media\": {\n      \"thumbnailUrl\": null,\n      \"imageUrl\": null,\n      \"imageUrls\": null,\n      \"videoUrl\": null,\n      \"videoHdUrl\": null,\n      \"durationSec\": null,\n      \"width\": null,\n      \"height\": null,\n      \"captionsUrl\": null\n    },\n    \"music\": null,\n    \"comments\": [],\n    \"transcript\": null\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_a2ef7bb2-67f4-436d-a56f-7a4d2ada9327\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1d0-1afc-7a37-8a7b-17c71b5bf81c\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"lookupStatus":"found","post":{"platform":"facebook","postId":"2817241591782952","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1723720494468406/posts/2817241591782952/","description":"Posting anonymous because our coaches retaliate against our kids for what we say.  \nHere's my question,  what can you do if the coaches are trying to hold you back? \nMy son has played football since he was 5. He can play every position and really well. He is just naturally athletic.  (Also played as pitcher, catcher and 3rd base on baseball,  played basketball,  soccer, wrestling,  lacrosse and always excelled). Football is his love and he wants to go pro so he gave up other sports and only fills in as guest player for tournaments in other sports off season as needed. He played offense and defense his freshman year staying in the whole game with no rest. He is a beast. He got to play a few varsity at the end of the year and has been a varsity starter sophomore and junior years. He has attended camps, combines, game day visits. He weight lifts. Puts film on Twitter and instagram.  Yet his coach won't promote him to scouts and said wait til next year. His senior year.  But they are promoting younger players (albeit they are specialty like running back, quarterback, kickers) who are now getting looked at.  \nIt's really deflating for a young player who has always given 100%. It makes them feel not good enough.  \nCoaches can make or break a player. Give them playtime or not. Get them scouted or overlooked.  \nWhat can we do as parents? I feel helpless.","publishedAt":"2025-11-03T14:20:51.000Z","isPaidPartnership":null,"sharedPostId":null,"sharedPostUrl":null,"feedbackId":"ZmVlZGJhY2s6cGZiaWQwMmRwaG9ZdXZXUUE4R3JRc1N5V1p6cHhncGtyOUFUNmlQdWFZbkxjVnBHaUpLMnNHRnFxbldnZ29QM0p5UzRyZHhs","linkAttachment":null},"author":{"name":"Anonymous participant","profileUrl":null,"avatarUrl":"https://scontent-iad3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35477-6/480704845_9249193088540936_1864352811635405115_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx160x160&ctp=s100x100&_nc_cat=1&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6f313d&_nc_ohc=dkVHLGVqEQMQ7kNvwHxu6vs&_nc_oc=AdqXhbfcsghdZdtbdwui4D0U8sLT-ByM5a-k10XGF5U3LRujDWOglSo1omL1wyvaJQ8&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.xx&_nc_gid=OJIIUvzSSSLAmeS-5Qd41w&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQStdlT6tpm32ayHsdEyiLoiaGG84eLbRYGGG7sCCoK9xg&oe=6AF3DA17","platformUserId":"6819074183269